# Don't forget in Russian: aspect after не
subtitle: "Не звони́ or не позвони́? Which aspect comes after не, не на́до, нельзя́ and начина́ть, as О́льга leaves Tom in charge of the kitchen."
tags: ["russian","russian aspect","не забудь","russian imperative","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/aspect","grammar/imperatives"]
thumb: "band \"Don't call — or mind you don't?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"I had to in Russian: пришлось, удалось, не хватает","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/136-russian-had-to.cast"}

## Don't forget in Russian: aspect after не
stress: new
level: basic
shuffle: true
heading: false

    icon tom size 130 set twemoji x 890 y 450 or ["cook","man"] icon_look picture of "man cook" hidden true
    text tom_name "Tom" #8f887c x 890 y 350 font_size 30 hidden true
    icon olga size 130 set twemoji x 110 y 450 or ["cook","woman"] icon_look picture of "woman cook" hidden true
    text olga_name "О́льга" #8f887c x 110 y 350 font_size 30 hidden true
